course: dictionary
lesson: 12889
title: Counting and listing things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enumeration is a formal word for counting or naming things one by one, in a careful order. «The coach made an enumeration of the team: Ava, Ben, Cara, Dev.» Each name is named once, in order, so none is missed.
explain: A numbered list is also an enumeration. «The sign gave an enumeration of the park rules: 1) no bikes, 2) no dogs, 3) no littering.» The numbers show the order, and the list covers every rule.
explain: In maths, enumeration means listing every possible case so you can count them all without missing any. «How many outfits can you make from 2 skirts and 2 tops?» Write each skirt with each top: that gives 4 outfits.
fact: Enumeration is a formal word, so you will meet it in rules, instructions and maths.
fact: Enumeration means counting or naming things one by one.
fact: A numbered or ordered list of things is an enumeration.
fact: In maths, enumeration means listing all the possibilities in a careful order, so none is missed.
fact: Censuses use enumerators, people who count everyone in a country.
exercise: «The coach made an enumeration of the team: Ava, Ben, Cara, Dev.» What is an enumeration? | A loud cheer for the winners | A small, sharp rock | *Counting or naming things one by one | A type of cake
exercise: Maya listed every outfit she could make from 2 skirts and 2 tops, so she would not miss one. What did she do? | Painted the skirts | *Made an enumeration of all the outfits | Wrote a poem about shoes | Forgot the tops
exercise: Which word means a numbered or ordered list of things? | Whisper | *Enumeration | Castle | Gentle
test: Ella wrote a list: «1) bring a pencil, 2) bring a ruler, 3) bring a rubber.» What kind of list is this? | A kind of puppet | A map of the school | *An enumeration, a numbered list | A song
test: In maths, what does enumeration mean? | Adding two numbers quickly | Drawing a big circle | Guessing a random number | *Listing all possible cases so none is missed
exam: A census counts everyone in a country. What are the people who do the counting called? | Pilots | Bakers | Gardeners | *Enumerators
